        <input type="text" name="Find" aria-label="Find Word Box" value="" style="padding: 5px; line-height: 12px; font-size: 12px;" /><input type="submit" value="Highlight Word" style="padding: 5px 15px; line-height: 12px; font-size: 12px;" /></form></td>
        			</tr>
        		</table>
        		<script language="javascript" type="text/javascript">
        	function checkChildren(srcObj, vType) {
        		for (var i = 0; i < eval("document.formSMC." + vType + ".length"); i++) {
        			if ((eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].value.substring(0, srcObj.length)") == srcObj) && (eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].disabled") == false)) {
        					(eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i].checked")) ? eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i]").checked = false : eval("document.formSMC." + vType + "[i]").checked = true;
        			}
        		}
        		return false;
        	}
        function toggleRepealed(element) {
        	const rows = document.getElementById("hideRepealed").querySelectorAll('tr');
        	rows.forEach(function (row) {
        		var text = row.textContent;		
        		if (text.includes('REPEALED') && !row.classList.contains('hidden')) {
        			row.classList.add('hidden')
        		}
        		else {
        			row.classList.remove('hidden')
        		}
        	})
        }
        function HideRepealed() {
        	const rows = document.getElementById("hideRepealed").querySelectorAll('tr');
        	rows.forEach(function (row) {
        		var text = row.textContent;		
        		if (text.includes('REPEALED') && !row.classList.contains('hidden')) {
        			row.classList.add('hidden')
        		}
        	})
        }
        </script>
        <div style="padding: 15px;"><form action="/smc/" method="post" name="formSMC">
        <div id="hideRepealed">
        		<p><a href="/smc/?Title=08">Title 08</a> Taxation and Revenue</p>
        				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=08.01">Chapter 08.01</a> Business Registrations</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=08.01.010">Section 08.01.010</a> Authority and Intent<br />
        <p>The provisions of this chapter are an exercise of the power of the City to regulate for revenue. It is the intent of the City that the provisions of this chapter prescribing regulation fees be liberally construed in favor of applicability of the regulation fees.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, October 8, 2012</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, October 15, 2012</p><p>ORD C34926 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=08.01.020">Section 08.01.020</a> Definitions<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Words are to be given their usual meaning except the following terms and their derivations have the meaning given when used in this chapter. When not inconsistent with the context, words used in the present tense include the future, words in the plural include the singular and words in the singular include the plural. The word &ldquo;shall&rdquo; is always mandatory and not merely directory.</span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Business&rdquo; includes all activities, occupations, trades, pursuits, professions, and matters located or engaged in within the city with the object of gain, benefit, or advantage to the registrant or to another person or class, directly or indirectly.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Business License Service&rdquo; means the office within the Washington State Department of Revenue handling the application for the City of Spokane general business licensing and issuing the document to registered taxpayers to display at the respective places of business.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Certified B Corporation&rdquo; means any for-profit company certified by the non-profit B Lab to meet rigorous standards of social and environmental performance, accountability, and transparency.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;City&rdquo; means the City of Spokane. </span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;City Council&rdquo; means the City Council of the City of Spokane</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Consumer show&rdquo; is an organized exhibition, display, or show that lasts for not more than five consecutive days and involves ten or more exhibitors It includes those events that partake the character of a unified display as well as those that are open to the public or limited to a prospective clientele It does not include shows exempted under&nbsp;<a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.01.090">SMC 8.01.090(C)</a>.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A consumer show includes events that may occur:</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">within a building,</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">within a connected set of buildings,</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">at parks or on grounds, or</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The term &ldquo;consumer show&rdquo; includes in addition to its common meaning any of the following:</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An antique show, boat show, sports show, arts and crafts or hobby show, agricultural show, street fair, festival, consumer show, horticultural show, or industrial show.</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An art exhibit, coin, stamp, or hobby show.</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A home show or recreational vehicle show.</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A commercial or business fair; or</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="5" style="list-style-type:lower-roman">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Any other show or exhibition of a similar nature.</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Consumer show&rdquo; excludes a farmer&rsquo;s market, &ldquo;flea&rdquo; market, antique mart, bazaar, or similar congregation of vendors and/or exhibitors that offer goods or services to the public at the same location on a recurrent basis more than four times per year or other events of similar character.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Engaging in business&rdquo; means commencing, conducting, or continuing in business, and also the exercise of corporate or franchise powers, as well as liquidating a business when the liquidators thereof hold themselves out to the public as conducting such business.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="8" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;General business license&rdquo; has the same meaning as &ldquo;General business license&rdquo; in RCW 35.090.010.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-roman">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Gross income&rdquo; means the total income to the registering entity from engaging in business within the city without any deductions for taxes, bad debt, or other deductions. It is not computed separately for each individual partner, principal, employee, or other constituent part of the registrant.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="10" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Insignia&rdquo;, or its singular number, &ldquo;insigne&rdquo;, is any tag, plate, badge, emblem, sticker or any other kind of device required for use in connection with any license.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="11" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Itinerant Vendor&rdquo;, as used in this section is defined in<a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.40.010">&nbsp;</a></span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.40.010"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 10.40.010</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="12" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;License&rdquo; includes the words &ldquo;permit&rdquo; or &ldquo;permittee&rdquo; means the general privilege or the holder of any privilege, respectively, under this code or other law or ordinance.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="13" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;License officer&rdquo; is the Chief Financial Officer or their designee, unless otherwise designated. </span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="14" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Nonprofit Corporation&rdquo; or &ldquo;Nonprofit Organization&rdquo; means a corporation, organization or limited liability corporation:</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Formed and organized under chapter 24.03 RCW, and</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">In accordance with Internal Revenue Code sections 501(c)(3) or 501(c)(4), and as hereafter amended.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Where the term nonprofit organization is used, it is meant to include a nonprofit corporation or nonprofit limited liability corporation.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="15" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Person&rdquo; or &ldquo;Persons&rdquo; is meant to include individual natural persons, partnerships, joint ventures, societies, associations, clubs, trustees, trusts, or corporations.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="16" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&quot;Personnel&quot; means any person employed by or working for any business located within the city, and/or persons who perform any part of their duties within the city. This includes officers, owners, agents, or other staff functions.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All officers, agents, dealers, LLC members, etc., of a corporation or business trust, and all partners of a partnership are counted as personnel within this definition.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A sole proprietor, owner and spouse are not counted as personnel.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Each part-time or each temporary person must be counted as one personnel.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Volunteers are not counted as personnel in determining the business registration fee.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="17" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Premises&rdquo; is meant to include all lands, structures, places, equipment, and appurtenances connected or used in any business, and any personal property or fixture used in connection with any business.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="18" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Registrant&rdquo; includes any person who:</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Engages in business,</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Is required to have a business license and/or registration,</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Is liable for any license fee, registration fee, or tax, or</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Performs any act for which a license fee, registration fee, or tax is imposed by this chapter.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="19" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Regulatory business license&rdquo; has the same meaning as &ldquo;Regulatory business license&rdquo; in RCW 35.090.010.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="20" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Social Purpose Corporation&rdquo; means a corporation that has elected to be governed as a social purpose corporation under chapter 23B.25 RCW.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36651 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=08.01.025">Section 08.01.025</a> REPEALED (Consumer Show Definitions) <br />
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36651 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=08.01.030">Section 08.01.030</a> REPEALED (Business)<br />
        <p>Repealed by Ordinance C34517.</p>
        <p>This section&nbsp;moved to <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.01.020">SMC 8.01.020</a>. </p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 30, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, January 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34517 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=08.01.040">Section 08.01.040</a> REPEALED (Personnel)<br />
        <p>Repealed by Ordinance C34517.</p>
        <p>This section&nbsp;moved to <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.01.020">SMC 8.01.020</a>. </p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 30, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, January 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34517 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=08.01.050">Section 08.01.050</a> REPEALED (Engaging in Business)<br />
        <p>Repealed by Ordinance C34517.</p>
        <p>This section&nbsp;moved to <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.01.020">SMC 8.01.020</a>. </p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 30, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, January 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34517 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=08.01.060">Section 08.01.060</a> REPEALED (Taxpayer)<br />
        <p>Repealed by Ordinance C34517.</p>
        <p>This section&nbsp;moved to <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.01.020">SMC 8.01.020</a>. </p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 30, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, January 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34517 Section 5</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=08.01.065">Section 08.01.065</a> REPEALED (Consumer Show Definitions)<br />
        <p>Repealed by Ordinance C34517.</p>
        <p>This section&nbsp;moved to <a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=08.01.025">SMC 8.01.025</a>. </p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, November 30, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, January 1, 2010</p><p>ORD C34517 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=08.01.070">Section 08.01.070</a> Business Registration Required<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">No person may engage in business in the city of Spokane or with the City without first having obtained and being the holder of a valid annual business registration&nbsp;or temporary business registration&nbsp;a Spokane city endorsement as provided in this chapter. Annual general business licenses with a Spokane city endorsement shall be issued and registered through the Washington State Department of Revenue&rsquo;s Business Licensing Service (BLS). A general business license is good for twelve months and must be renewed before expiration&nbsp;for the next twelve months. Any temporary registrations, to include itinerant vendor registrations<u>,</u> shall be issued and registered by the City of Spokane Taxes and Licenses Office. In addition, persons whose activities fall within the definition of&nbsp;<a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.40.010" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline">SMC 10.40.010</a>&nbsp;must obtain an &ldquo;itinerant vendor&rdquo; permit as provided in&nbsp;<a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.40.010" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline">SMC 10.40.010</a>, in addition to a business registration. A business license does not authorize illegal activities.</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">If a business changes names or locations during a registration&nbsp;year, it must notify the Washington State Business Licensing Service to obtain a new registration&nbsp;document to display in the place of business that reflects the change of name or location. A change of location&nbsp;may require the filing of a new application&nbsp;through the Business Licensing Service, as described in this chapter.</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif">A person or business conducting the following activities shall register for an annual regulatory business license or obtain an annual permit in addition to obtaining a general business license and shall follow the requirements of the activity&#39;s respective chapter:</span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <table align="center" border="1" cellspacing="0" class="Table" style="background:white; border-collapse:collapse; border:undefined">
        	<tbody>
        		<tr>
        			<td style="background-color:white; height:41.4pt">
